  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "The current best (config_001, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted in multiprofile mode. The single largest unexplored variable is the RNA encoder: we have only tested scvi_n200 across all three completed experiments. config_043 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) is a clean single-variable swap of the RNA encoder while holding all other components at their best-performing settings. This directly tests whether scgpt can match or exceed scvi_n200 in the top architecture, reducing uncertainty about a core design choice before we invest remaining budget in fine-tuning other axes (aggregation, profile setting, image encoder). If scgpt performs comparably, it opens a broader search space; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as critical and we can focus remaining experiments on aggregation and profile-setting variants. Expected cost: moderate, roughly 4–5 GPU hours (scgpt is slightly heavier than scvi_n200, but the imagenet_vit_l + transformer pipeline matches config_001's 3.60 h baseline, so the total should be in a similar or slightly higher range)."
}

